WEBVTT

00:08:28.493 --> 00:08:31.393
The Congressional Buildings Act of 1910

00:08:31.417 --> 00:08:33.351
limits the height of buildings in D.C.

00:08:33.375 --> 00:08:35.309
to 130 feet,

00:08:35.333 --> 00:08:38.184
except for spires, towers,
domes and minarets.

00:08:38.208 --> 00:08:42.851
This pretty much exempts monuments
of the church and state.

00:08:42.875 --> 00:08:45.976
And the bubble is 153 ft.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.601
That's the Pantheon next to it.

00:08:48.625 --> 00:08:51.893
It's about 1.2 million cubic
feet of compressed air.

00:08:51.917 --> 00:08:53.809
And so we argued it

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:55.809
on the merits of being a dome.

00:08:55.833 --> 00:08:57.893
So there it is,

00:08:57.917 --> 00:08:59.067
very stately,

00:08:59.091 --> 00:09:02.518
among all the stately
buildings in the Mall.